From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Vikhammer <marius.vikhammer@espressif.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:24:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(freertos): place pxPortGetCoprocArea in IRAM

rtos_int_enter calls it to save the HWLP context of the
interrupted task. With CONFIG_FREERTOS_IN_IRAM=n it was in
flash, so an IRAM interrupt arriving while the cache was
disabled, with the HWLP state dirty, caused a cache error
panic on ESP32-P4 and ESP32-S31.

Closes https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf/issues/19308

Upstream: b3b3caf2e98 (master)
---
 components/freertos/linker.lf | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/components/freertos/linker.lf b/components/freertos/linker.lf
index a690ca11ffe..82e68b6220b 100644
--- a/components/freertos/linker.lf
+++ b/components/freertos/linker.lf
@@ -150,6 +150,8 @@ entries:
         #   - vPortSetStackWatchpoint is called from vTaskSwitchContext, which is in IRAM.
         # - vPortCoprocUsedInISR is directly called from RISC-V assembly code with a direct branch instruction which
         #   may be too far when placed in Flash. Hence, it is always placed in internal RAM
+        # - pxPortGetCoprocArea is called by rtos_int_enter to save the HWLP context of the interrupted task, so it
+        #   must be in IRAM for interrupts that run while the cache is disabled.
         # - The following functions are called from an ISR context, thus are placed in IRAM unless ISR functions are
         #   placed into flash.
         #   - xPortInIsrContext
@@ -166,6 +168,8 @@ entries:
             port:vPortYieldOtherCore (noflash_text)
             port:vPortSetStackWatchpoint (noflash_text)
             port:vPortCoprocUsedInISR (noflash_text)
+            if SOC_CPU_COPROC_NUM > 0:
+                port:pxPortGetCoprocArea (noflash_text)
             if FREERTOS_UNICORE = n:
                 port:xPortEnterCriticalTimeout (noflash_text)
                 port:vPortExitCriticalMultiCore (noflash_text)
